 "result_text": "I fixed `SSHTunnelForwarder.get_keys` in `sshtunnel.py` so it searches the default SSH directory when you don't pass `host_pkey_directories`. I only checked that the module imports. I didn't run the test suite or try it against a real `~/.ssh`.\n\nThe cause was the `if host_pkey_directories is not None:` guard. With the default of `None`, the whole key search was skipped, so the `or [DEFAULT_SSH_DIRECTORY]` fallback never ran.\n\nThe check is now `if not host_pkey_directories:`, which sets the list to `[DEFAULT_SSH_DIRECTORY]`. An empty list also falls back to the default, as the old `or` did. The rest of the loop is unchanged apart from losing one level of indentation.",
